{"id":"H5042","lemma":"נָבַע","transliteration":"nava","sayIt":"na-va","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to bubble","meaning":"1) to flow, pour out, pour, gush forth, spring, bubble up, ferment\n1a) (Qal) to flow\n1b)(Hiphil) to pour out, emit, cause to bubble, belch forth\n1b1) to pour out\n1b2) to cause to bubble, ferment\n1b3) to pour forth, emit, belch forth","glosses":["pour forth","spew","utter","pour out","extol","would have poured out"],"count":11,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"psa-19","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"they pour forth","kjv":"uttereth"}},{"chapterId":"psa-59","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"they spew","kjv":"they belch out"}},{"chapterId":"psa-78","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"I will utter","kjv":"I will utter"}},{"chapterId":"psa-94","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"They pour out","kjv":"How long shall they utter"}},{"chapterId":"psa-119","v":171,"renderings":{"bsb":"pour forth","kjv":"shall utter"}},{"chapterId":"psa-145","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"They will extol","kjv":"They shall abundantly utter"}},{"chapterId":"pro-1","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"I would have poured out","kjv":"I will pour out"}},{"chapterId":"pro-15","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"spouts","kjv":"poureth out"}},{"chapterId":"pro-15","v":28,"renderings":{"bsb":"blurts out","kjv":"poureth"}},{"chapterId":"pro-18","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"is a bubbling","kjv":"as a flowing"}},{"chapterId":"ecc-10","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"bring","kjv":"to send forth"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Psalm 19:2","note":"Day after day they pour out speech, and night after night they display knowledge.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Proverbs 1:23","note":"Turn at my reproof. Behold, I will pour out my spirit on you. I will make known my words to you.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Ecclesiastes 10:1","note":"Dead flies cause the oil of the perfumer to produce an evil odor; so does a little folly outweigh wisdom and honor.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible T